{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass.</b> Your [fem.] valleys — facing Jerusalem." "<b>Set in array.</b> The siege mound and the engines of war."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads עמקיך as feminine singular ('your valley') addressed to the Valley of Vision (Jerusalem); the sense is that the enemy's divisions filled the valley facing the city."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:37.252866787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}